**Question Title:** Create a Project Folder Structure

**Question Link:**  
https://my.newtonschool.co/playground/code/jipp2htnvrww?lecture_hash=v210chxjexei

**Solution:**
```bash
cat > create-service << 'EOF'
#!/bin/bash

mkdir -p service/controllers
mkdir -p service/models
mkdir -p service/routes
mkdir -p service/middleware

echo "API Service" > service/README.md
echo 'console.log("Server started");' > service/server.js
EOF

chmod +x create-service
./create-service
```

**Approach:**

1. Writing the required commands into the `create-service` file by replacing its existing incorrect code.

2. Making the `create-service` file executable by granting it execution permission.

3. Running the `create-service` script to generate the required service directory structure and files.

**Result:**
```text
service/
├── controllers/
├── models/
├── routes/
├── middleware/
├── server.js
└── README.md
```

The required service directory structure was successfully created.